{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the one who carries.</b> [This is] more stringent than the one who touches; therefore he must wash his garments, even though [not] his body. And likewise the rule for every animal. Here too he held to a concise path, and so it is: 'and wholly divides the hoof' [but] does not bring up the cud, or brings up the cud [but] does not wholly divide the hoof. And he already said, 'and you shall not touch their carcasses; they are unclean to you.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Omitted 'not' before 'his body' hyper-literally; the Hebrew אף כי גופו is elliptical, meaning the carrier washes garments even though his body [is not required to be washed]. The antecedent of 'he' in 'he held to a concise path' and 'he already said' is Moses, per Ibn Ezra's standard usage."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:32.375067028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}